From de47d5967cfa72feda848ffd5c588c9624b733a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron <aahladky@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 21:07:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] M4: SLRU policy, admission, prefill protection,
 projection-aware cache

SLRU (Segmented LRU):
- Probationary (20%) and protected (80%) segments
- New entries start in probationary; promote to protected on 2nd access
- Protected slots only evicted when protected segment is full
- Evict LRU probationary first, then demote LRU protected

Second-miss admission:
- --moe-cache-admission-misses N (default 1)
- Expert must be missed N times before promotion
- Prevents one-off experts from evicting hot entries

Prefill protection:
- set_phase(true) during prefill skips miss counting
- Long prompts don't flood the cache with one-use experts
- moe_cache_set_phase_all() exposed for server integration

Projection-aware cache:
- filled_mask tracks gate/up/down per slot independently
- lookup() takes projection param, returns hit only if filled
- promote_projection() copies just one projection per call
- mul_mat_id calls promote_projection on miss for the current projection

Verified on host (Qwen3.5-35B, 200 tokens, 1 GiB budget):
- SYCL0: 41,570 hits, 110,710 misses, 9,190 promotions, 6,807 evictions
- Hit rate 27.3% (cache warming up), all 2,383 slots filled
- SLRU policy working: evictions happen only when cache is full
